WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.580
- Well, I'm a huge "Parks
and Recreation" fan

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.100
and I have a very embarrassing confession.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.630
I told him backstage,
but in 2011 I tweeted,

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:11.610
I didn't just tweet,

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.540
I begged to be on "Parks and Recreation"

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.960
just so I could be in a
scene with Ron Swanson

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.280
because I was obsessed.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.113
Here's the thing.

00:00:20.113 --> 00:00:21.590
I even owned that I was a horrible actor.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:22.680
I'm a horrible actor.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.512
But I have a lot of spirit

00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:27.390
(audience laughs)
and I could've played

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:28.223
a bad actor.

00:00:28.223 --> 00:00:30.240
I didn't get a call, it's fine, it's fine.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.060
Amy, it's fine, y'all.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.420
No, but if we could
turn back time with Cher

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.530
and you gave me a role,
- If we could find a way.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.490
- what do you think I could've played?

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:45.220
Maybe a stage five
cleaner for Ron Swanson.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.140
- It's a huge compliment, first of all.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.730
I'm very grateful that you
wanted to be on the show.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.500
- Dude, it's great, it was so great.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.646
There's so many great actors on there.

00:00:53.646 --> 00:00:56.430
- I was grateful to get
to go to work every day

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:00.830
and I think great comedy
writers, they look at me

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:03.977
and they say, "We can make
people laugh with this.

00:01:03.977 --> 00:01:06.637
"With these raw materials.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:06.637 --> 00:01:08.987
"Give that guy a coffee cup.

00:01:08.987 --> 00:01:10.787
"Oh yeah, here we go.

00:01:10.787 --> 00:01:13.080
"Give him a phone on his belt."

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.760
- You know what, the
physical comedy is so key.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:16.830
- It is.
- That's what's so great.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.430
- But I think they would look at you.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:20.467
So they take your strengths
and they would say,

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:25.437
"Okay, let's cast Kelly
as a very enthusiastic,

00:01:25.437 --> 00:01:29.814
"wildly enthusiastic
hurricane of positivity."

00:01:29.814 --> 00:01:31.340
- Yes.
- And I think the laugh

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:34.070
to get with a Kelly Clarkson character is

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.830
someone who would out-Leslie
Knope Leslie Knope.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.611
- Exactly.
- You would finally--

00:01:39.611 --> 00:01:42.930
- Where were you in 2011?
- Someone would go too far.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.630
- I'm just kidding.
- Somebody who Leslie Knope

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.009
would be like, "She's too much."

00:01:47.009 --> 00:01:47.842
- [Kelly] She's a little

00:01:47.842 --> 00:01:48.675
over the top.
- She's too excited.

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:51.420
- You know what, not the
first time I've heard that.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.880
Probably not the last.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.100
My husband says it every night

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.930
and then he says, "I love you."

